      "heading_context": "## Gotchas from C#",
      "headers": [
        "C# behavior",
        "Go behavior",
        "Consequence"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`List<T>` is always a reference",
          "Slice is a reference to backing array — sub-slices share backing",
          "Modifying sub-slice modifies original"
        ],
        [
          "`Dictionary<K,V>` readable when null",
          "Writing to nil map **panics**",
          "Initialize with `make`"
        ],
        [
          "Classes have inheritance",
          "Go has no inheritance — use composition (embedding)",
          "Different OOP model"
        ],
        [
          "Multiple return not idiomatic",
          "Multiple return values are idiomatic `(T, error)`",
          "Learn to love it"
        ],
        [
          "`try/catch`",
          "`if err != nil` on every call",
          "More verbose; more explicit"
        ],
        [
          "`using` for cleanup",
          "`defer` for cleanup",
          "`defer` runs at function end, not block end"
        ],
        [
          "Ternary `cond ? a : b`",
          "No ternary",
          "Write the if/else"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-4",
      "line": 573,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Decision",
        "Use X",
        "When Y"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**goroutine vs `sync.WaitGroup` vs channel**",
          "goroutine alone",
          "Fire-and-forget; result not needed by caller"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "goroutine + `WaitGroup`",
          "Fan-out work; need to know when all are done; no inter-goroutine data"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "goroutine + channel",
          "Goroutines need to communicate results back; pipeline patterns"
        ],
        [
          "**pointer receiver vs value receiver**",
          "pointer receiver `(p *T)`",
          "Method mutates the struct; struct is large (avoid copy cost)"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "value receiver `(p T)`",
          "Read-only method; small struct; consistency when T has no pointer methods"
        ],
        [
          "**`errors.Is` vs `errors.As` vs type assertion**",
          "`errors.Is(err, target)`",
          "Check for a specific sentinel error value anywhere in the chain"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "`errors.As(err, &target)`",
          "Unwrap chain looking for a specific error type; extract its fields"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "type assertion `err.(*MyErr)`",
          "Direct type check without unwrapping; only use when not using `%w` wrapping"
        ],
        [
          "**`interface{}` / `any` vs generics**",
          "`interface{}` / `any`",
          "Pre-Go 1.18 code; truly heterogeneous containers; `fmt`-style variadic"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "generics `[T constraint]`",
          "Type-safe algorithms over multiple types; avoid `interface{}` + type assertion boilerplate"
        ],
        [
          "**`make` vs `new` vs composite literal**",
          "`make(T, ...)`",
          "Slices, maps, channels — initializes internal structure (len/cap/buffer)"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "`new(T)`",
          "Allocates zeroed T and returns `*T`; rarely needed; prefer composite literal"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "`T{...}` composite literal",
          "Structs, arrays, slices, maps with known values; most readable"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
